<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kahramanmaraş</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Maraş, Marqas, Germanicia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kahramanmaraş is a city in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains">Taurus Mountains</a>. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> it was Marqas, capital of the Neo-Hittite kingdom of Gurgum, and later, as Germanicia and then Maraş, it was a frontier town between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> and the Islamic world. It received the epithet Kahraman, 'heroic', for its resistance to French occupation in 1920, and it was badly hit by the earthquakes of February 2023.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kahramanmaras.jpg" alt="Kahramanmaraş" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Myrat · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kahramanmara%C5%9F_city_center.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Around them gathered the Saadlu, Karamanlu, Alpaut, Agacheri, Dukharlu, Jagirlu and Hajilu tribes, from Nakhchivan and Ganja to <b>Maraş</b>, Erzurum and Ardabil; their own traditions say they came to Anatolia from Central Asia with the Mongol conquest.</blockquote><a href="/empire/qara-qoyunlu">Qara Qoyunlu · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>An earthquake with an estimated magnitude of 7.4 to 7.7 struck the area of Marash, now <b>Kahramanmaraş</b>, and also hit Antioch, Mamistra and Edessa in the crusader lands.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-29">29 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Ala al-Dawla Bozkurt, a long-reigning ruler, built in <b>Marash</b> and resisted the rising Safavids.</blockquote><a href="/state/dulkadirids">Dulkadirids</a></li><li><blockquote>The administration encouraged Armenian resettlement in Adana, <b>Marash</b> and Aintab, which alarmed Turkish Muslims.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-cilicia">French Cilicia</a></li><li><blockquote>Gurgum arose after the Hittite collapse in the valley of the Aksu river around <b>Marqas</b>, modern Kahramanmaraş, in south-eastern Turkey.</blockquote><a href="/state/gurgum">Gurgum</a></li><li><blockquote>After the defeat at Manzikert in 1071 and the civil wars that followed, he gathered soldiers and Armenian refugees and made himself master of <b>Marash</b>, Melitene and other towns in the Taurus and Cilicia.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-philaretos-brachamios">Principality of Philaretos Brachamios</a></li></ul></section>
